// An instance of a generic procedure is the program's, whichever file
// calls it (issue #226, spec 7.11): negate, which a #loaded file declares,
// is called with a bool from this file and from that one. Its one instance
// for bool is checked once: its error, in the loaded file, is said once,
// its chain naming the call in this file that made it, and the loaded
// file's call of the same instance says nothing more.
#load "load/generic_files.rig";

main :: () {
    x := negate(true);
    y := from_loaded();
}
